course: dictionary
lesson: 13961
title: Comparing with liken
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To liken one thing to another means to say they are alike. You are comparing them. «Ravi likens his little sister to a noisy alarm clock.» Ravi is not saying she is a clock. He means she is loud, like one.
explain: Look for the word «to» after liken. «Liken A to B» means say A is similar to B. «The poet likens the moon to a silver coin.» The moon is round and shiny, like a coin, so the poet makes that comparison.
explain: Writers use liken in stories and poems. People also use it in science and history: «Doctors often liken the heart to a pump.» The past form is likened, as in «The old tree was likened to a giant umbrella.»
fact: Liken is a verb. Its forms are likens, likened and likening.
fact: Liken means to compare one thing with another.
fact: «Liken A to B» means say A is similar to B.
fact: «The moon was likened to a silver coin.»
fact: Compare means much the same as liken, so it can help you check the meaning.
exercise: «The poet likens the moon to a silver coin.» What does liken mean here? | To lose a coin in the dark | *To compare the moon with a coin | To buy a silver ring | To paint the moon gold
exercise: Ravi says, «My brother likens his bedroom to a pigsty.» What is Ravi saying? | He wants a new pigsty for the garden | He has just cleaned the bedroom | He thinks his brother is a pig | *He thinks the bedroom looks very messy, like a pigsty
exercise: Which word means about the same as liken? | *Compare | Shout | Forget | Hide
test: «Doctors often liken the heart to a pump.» What does this sentence tell you? | Doctors think the heart is like a pump | Doctors have a pump in their surgery | The heart stops working after a pump | *The heart and a pump are similar in some way
test: Which sentence uses liken correctly? | The puppy likens the dinner. | Mum likens to the puppy the door. | *Mum likens the new puppy to a ball of fluff. | Mum likened she went home.
exam: «The writer likened the waves to galloping horses.» What does likened mean? | Ran away from the horses | Counted the waves | Swam quickly across the sea | *Compared the waves to horses
